CON_0090	PID_0068	rda_graph:PID_0068	Leveraging PIDs for object management in data infrastructures		https://zenodo.org/records/3361619				DOI	https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3361619	2019-08-06	Multiple recommendations of the Research Data Alliance (RDA) can be combined to help improve workflows in research infrastructures related to the management of FAIR Digital Objects. In the concrete example given, the background motivational case is from climate research data and its supporting infrastructure services, but other cases have been part of RDA discussions. More specifically, the presentation shows how under the umbrella of the Data Fabric concept, the recommendations of PID Kernel Information, Data Type Registries and Research Data Collections can be leveraged to support object management. Persistent Identifiers (PIDs), metadata and knowledge graphs built with them are key concepts that are part of such a solution.	eng	publication-presentation	info:eu-repo/semantics/presentation		\N	\N	\N	\N
