CON_0105	PID_0078	rda_graph:PID_0078	New version of the DMP Common Standard Ontology	DMP Common Standards WG Discussions DMP Common Standards Ontology	https://zenodo.org/records/3944464		https://www.rd-alliance.org/groups/dmp-common-standards-wg/forum/topic/dmp-common-standards-ontology/		DOI	https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3944463	2020-07-14	The development of the DMP Common Standard Ontology (DCSO) is an ongoing effort intended to provide semantic technology representation of the DCS application profile.\n\nThis report is a summary of work done by the Unaturals team at the RDA Hackathon on machine-actionable Data Management Plans that took place between 27th and 29th May 2020\n\n\nThe objective of this Issue was to create a new version of the DCSO that complies with the best practices in the community. For this hackathon there were 3 main sub-issues to tackle: (1) Third-party concept integration; (2) controlled vocabularies; and (3) constraint representation.\n	eng	publication-report	info:eu-repo/semantics/report		\N	\N	\N	\N
CON_0106	PID_0079	rda_graph:PID_0079	Online Survey for DMP-Guidance from Research Data Alliance Working Group Discipline-specific Guidance for DMP		https://zenodo.org/records/7443373				DOI	https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7443372	2022-12-15	Data management plans, as required by institutional or research funding agencies, are often very general and lack meaningful discipline-specific adaptations. The Research Data Alliance's Discipline-Specific Guidance for Data Management Plans Working Group aims to address this gap and develop appropriate guidance and recommendations.\n\n\nThis survey, sent to researchers, data managers, and RDM-supporting infrastructures, serves as the basis. The online survey was conducted using the open-source software SoSciSurvey and was open for data collection from November 8, 2021 to January 14, 2022.\n\nThe survey was divided into the following areas after a brief introduction on "Purpose of this survey" and "Use of the information you provide."\n\n\n\tDemographics\n\tData Description and Collection\n\tData Documentation & Quality\n\tData Archiving, Publishing & Sharing After the Project\n\tGuidelines, Principles & Best Practices\n\tFollow-up interviews and group discussions\n\n\nThe analysis of the online survey was focused on the four areas: Natural Sciences, Life Sciences, Humanities & Social Sciences, and Engineering. The results of the evaluation will be presented in a separate publication.\n\nThe resulting data can be accessed here: DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.7391669\n\nThe data were evaluated using R. The code is published under the following DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.7443467\n\nA more detailed analysis and description can be found in the paper "Discipline-specific Aspects in Data Management Planning" submitted to Data Science Journal (2022-12-15).	eng	publication-proposal	info:eu-repo/semantics/proposal		\N	\N	\N	\N
